# SDLC (PersonaLearn)

Follow the `sdlc-pr-lifecycle` skill for the procedure. Fill Issues and Jira bodies from the repo templates. PR bodies follow the `writing-prs` skill. Issue and Jira headings are in `docs/sdlc-writing-standard.md`.

## Systems

| System | Owns |
|--------|------|
| **Jira (PSL)** | Tickets, sprint, status, blockers |
| **Confluence (PLEARN)** | Specs, ADRs, release notes, retros |
| **GitHub** | Code, branches, PRs, CI, release tags |
| **Slack (#personalearn-dev)** | Notifications only |

Notion is outside this chain. Confluence pages use the native blueprints (Product requirements, Decision documentation, Status update, Retrospective). Hub: https://nervustechnologies.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLEARN/overview

Issue → `PSL-N` → spec → branch/PR → Slack. A feature or bug needs the Issue (`needs-triage`, best-guess `type-*`, assignee, milestone) before a ticket, a branch, or implementation.

## Branch and commit

Never implement on `develop` or `main`. Fetch `origin/develop` and branch from it, or from the merged prerequisite. A hotfix branches from `main` instead; see Hotfix. Reuse an existing ticket branch.

| Work | Branch prefix | Commit prefix |
|------|---------------|---------------|
| Feature | `feature/` | `feat:` |
| Bug | `fix/` | `fix:` |
| Chore | `chore/` | `chore:` |
| Docs | `docs/` | `docs:` |

Branch: `{prefix}/PSL-{n}-{short-kebab-description}`. Subject: `{prefix} … (PSL-N)`. Stage only that ticket’s files. Never commit secrets.

One ticket, one branch, one PR. Dependent tickets merge to `develop` in order; the next branch then rebases.

## Hotfix

Use `hotfix/PSL-<n>-<slug>` only when production is broken or at risk (a P1) and the fix should not wait behind unreleased work on `develop`. Branch it from `main`. Everything else stays `feature/` or `fix/` into `develop`.

The pull request targets `main`. A human approves the merge. A merge to `main` deploys Vercel production, so preview QA is required before merging.

After the merge, open a back-merge pull request from `main` into `develop`, or cherry-pick the fix, so `develop` keeps it.

## Ticket descriptions

Do not repeat metadata that already has its own field: labels, priority, assignee, milestone, sprint, points, dates.

A description holds the problem, the context, short acceptance criteria, and links that are not already linked.

The PR test plan lives in `.github/pull_request_template.md`. Merge gates live in this file, not in every ticket.

## The human approves commits and merges

The agent proposes; the human approves. Do not commit, push, or merge unless the human asked. Propose one focused slice and wait. A green build is not a commit, and an open pull request is not a merge.

## Pull request and release

PRs target `develop`. A hotfix targets `main`; see Hotfix. Rebase onto the base branch first. The title includes `PSL-N`. The Test plan lists only steps that were run.

One area and one type on the ticket and the PR: `area-auth`, `area-dashboard`, `area-classes`, `area-ai-rag`, `area-infra`, `area-docs`, and `type-feature`, `type-bug`, `type-chore`, `type-tech-debt`. Not GitHub’s `bug` or `enhancement`.

Default assignee is `raphaelmalims`. Set the assignee, the milestone (current sprint, otherwise `Backlog`), and the labels in the same step that creates the issue or pull request, on the Cursor creation path that already sets labels. Do not follow up with `gh pr edit` or `gh api` from the in-VM `cursor[bot]` (`ghs_`) token. That call returns 403 `Resource not accessible by integration`. If a field still cannot be set at creation, say so in the final report and leave it for the reviewer. Do not retry with `gh`.

Request a reviewer other than the author when another reviewer exists. If the only candidate is the author, skip the request. GitHub cannot self-review.

Before approve or merge:

- Walk every acceptance criterion on the GitHub Issue and on Jira, and tick each met box on both. A review comment does not replace those checkboxes.
- Every listed Test plan step is `[x]`.
- CI is green.
- The Vercel preview is healthy.

Squash-merge into `develop` and delete the branch. A hotfix merges to `main` first; see Hotfix. Do not self-approve. Close the linked Issue as completed.

Promote `develop` to `main` with a merge commit, then tag `v0.x.0`.

Also ask before scope past the ticket, before an untriaged Jira ticket, and before a branch with no GitHub Issue.
